<title>GREECE: Delos, Intern'l lead Greek balanced fund returns.</title>
<headline>Delos, Intern'l lead Greek balanced fund returns.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delos and International led Greece's 14 equity income mutual fund returns in end-February with year-to-date gains of 33.2 and 28.3 percent respectively, the association of institutional investors said in its monthly review.</p>
<p>It provided the following rankings:</p>
<p>    FUND		  ASSETS	CHANGE IN    RETURN (YTD)*</p>
<p>			    (drs bln)    SHARES**</p>
<p>1.  Delos		    21.2	 -4.8%	     33.2%</p>
<p>2.  International	   0.7	 14.9%	     28.3%</p>
<p>3.  Alpha		     1.4	  4.5%	     26.8%</p>
<p>4.  Triton		    1.4	 -0.1%	     24.6%</p>
<p>5.  Allianz		   2.9	  4.3%	     22.6%</p>
<p>6.  Helvetia		  1.4	  4.2%	     22.0%</p>
<p>7.  Delphi		    3.6	  4.2%	     21.8%</p>
<p>8.  National Insurance    1.5	 -6.2%	     16.5%</p>
<p>9.  Eurostar		  0.5	 -8.6%	     14.8%</p>
<p>10  Interamerican	   5.3	 -5.5%	     14.6%</p>
<p>11. Vergina		   2.0	  4.0%	     12.8%</p>
<p>12. Astir		     0.8	  0.9%	     11.4%</p>
<p>13. Bank of Attica	  0.5	  7.3%	     11.3%</p>
<p>14. Hermes		    2.7	 -0.1%	     11.1%</p>
<p>*  Returns are based on NAV on February 28</p>
<p>** Change in the number of shares measures</p>
<p>	 inflows/redemptions in February.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
